00:09:19,891 --> 00:09:21,041
Fail of the Week.

62
00:09:21,041 --> 00:09:24,953
"The Sora API Was Just Shut Down - No Grace Period"

63
00:09:24,953 --> 00:09:39,003
OpenAI permanently discontinued the Sora API (including sora-2 and sora-2-pro) on September 24, 2026, without a precise time and without a fixed final export deadline .

64
00:09:39,003 --> 00:09:44,366
Download links for generated videos were valid for a maximum of one hour after creation .

65
00:09:44,366 --> 00:09:56,966
Users had to back up videos, prompts, reference images, and project files themselves; unused credits can only be carried over to Codex, with no automatic refund or transfer to other providers .

66
00:09:56,966 --> 00:10:11,028
Root Cause: The API shutdown followed the closure of the web and app versions back in April 2026, without OpenAI providing a clear, communicated migration path for API customers with ongoing projects .

67
00:10:11,028 --> 00:10:20,741
What we're learning: If you build production workflows on a single API, you need an export automation in place from day one - never rely on a vendor's grace period.

